\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold the servant of the Lord!
\par I wait Thy guiding eye to feel,
\par To hear and keep Thy word,
\par To prove and do Thy perfect will,
\par Joyful from my own words to cease,
\par Glad to fulfil all righteousness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Me, if Thy grace vouchsafe to use,
\par Meanest of all Thy creatures, me:
\par The deed, the time, the manner choose,
\par Let all my fruit be found of Thee;
\par Let all my words in Thee be wrought,
\par By Thee to full perfection brought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My every weak, though good design,
\par O,errule, or change, as seems Thee meet;
\par Jesus, let all my work be Thine!
\par Thy work, O Lord, is all complete,
\par And pleasing in Thy Father's sight;
\par Thou only hast done all things right.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Here then to Thee Thy own I leave;
\par Mould as Thou wilt Thy passive clay;
\par But let me all Thy stamp receive,
\par But let me all Thy words obey,
\par Serve with a single heart and eye,
\par And to Thy glory live and die.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

